s downloadable by monthly, quarterly and annual statistics including trend analysis.\\n\\nYTD 2026 statistics (through March 2026) include:\\n\\n- Total equity issuance $58.8 billion, -0.5% Y/Y\\n\\n- IPO issuance $10.4 billion, +18.2% Y/Y\\n\\n- ADV 20.0 billion shares, +27.3% Y/Y\\n\\n- S&P 500 (end of period) 6,528.52, +16.3% Y/Y\\n\\n- VIX (average) 20.44%, +1.82 pps Y/Y\\n\\nGet notified when new data posts. Subscribe to our [email alerts](https://pages.sifma.org/sifma-research-and-insights).\\n\\n## Related Resources\\nSIFMA Research\\n\\n### Research Quarterly: Equities & Related\\n\\nThe SIFMA Research Quarterlies contain data and statistics on U.S. markets. The equity and related report – cash equites, ETFs, options and capital formation – includes information on: volumes, volatility, total equity issuance, IPOs, market shares, exchange landscapes, etc.\\n\\nPolicy & Regulation\\n\\n### Capital Formation\\n\\nThe ability of companies to raise capital efficiently is the foundation of U.S. economic growth. Capital formation enables businesses to expand, innovate, hire, and compete, while providing investors with opportunities to build wealth and support the broader economy.\\n\\nPolicy & Regulation\\n\\n### Equity Market Structure\\n\\nThe U.S. equity markets are the most robust in the world – deep, competitive, liquid, efficient, and transparent. They are also among the most highly regulated, playing a vital role in capital formation and investor confidence.\\n\\nGet the latest trends, stats, and research on financial markets and securities.\\n\\nSIFMA is the voice of the U.S. securities industry. We advocate for effective and resilient capital markets.\\n\\n© 2026 Securities Industry and Financial Markets Association.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e55c7a608b5df6d2\\\">>>\"\n}"}], "details": {"url": "https://www.sifma.org/research/statistics/us-equity-and-related-securities-statistics", "finalUrl": "https://www.sifma.org/research/statistics/us-e